= The fall of Cuno

By August the mark is worth almost nothing. A printing dispute in Berlin on 10 August, taken up and widened by the KPD, spreads to the factories, the factory councils meet, and in the streets the cry is "Cuno must go". The SPD, which had tolerated the government, withdraws its support in the Reichstag, and on 12 August Chancellor Cuno resigns. On the 13th Gustav Stresemann forms a Great Coalition of the SPD, Centre, DDP and DVP.

The question for the party was what to do when the strike began. A party that waits for a revolutionary situation to call a strike will be told it was late. A party that calls one at the wrong time will be told it was a fool.

- @strike: Call for a political general strike, with the factory councils in the lead.
- @support: Support the councils without issuing a call of our own.

